Explanation of the change:

- We call `Prism.languages.insertBefore('typescript', 'keyword', { … })` to define a new token named `property`.  
- The regex `/\b[_$a-zA-Z\xA0-\uFFFF][$\w\xA0-\uFFFF]*\??(?=\s*:)/` matches any valid identifier (plus an optional `?`) that is immediately followed by a colon.  
- Because it is inserted *before* the existing `keyword` rule, `type?` in `type?: string` will now be captured as `property` and will no longer be colored as a keyword.
